-- title:
--   Special-fibre package for the resolution of uv = varpi^e
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring that is a domain, let $\varpi \in O$ satisfy $\mathfrak m_O = (\varpi)$, let $e \in \mathbb N$, and let $F_0,\dots,F_e$ be ideal sheaf data on the scheme `Resolution ϖ e`, the colimit of the gluing diagram whose charts are copies of $\operatorname{Spec} (O[x,y]/(xy-\varpi))$, equipped with its maps `Resolution.toCrossing` to $\operatorname{Spec}(O[u,v]/(uv-\varpi^e))$ and `Resolution.toSpec` to $\operatorname{Spec} O$. Assume the chart table: for every $i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,e$ and every $k$, the pullback of $F_k$ along the $i$-th chart map `Resolution.ι ϖ e i` is the ideal sheaf generated by the image, under the inverse of the global-sections isomorphism, of $(V\varpi)$ if $k=i$, of $(U\varpi)$ if $k=i+1$, and of the unit ideal otherwise. The conclusion is the conjunction of seven assertions. (i) Each $F_k$ is invertible in the sense of the predicate `IsInvertible`: every point has an affine open neighbourhood $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with the point in the basic open of $f$, such that on the affine basic open of $f$ the ideal of $F_k$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor. (ii) $\prod_k F_k$ is the ideal sheaf generated by the global section of `Resolution ϖ e` obtained by pulling $\varpi$ back along `Resolution.toSpec`. (iii) $\prod_k F_k^{\,k}$ is the ideal sheaf generated by the pullback of $U(\varpi^e)$ along `Resolution.toCrossing`. (iv) Every point in the support of any $F_k$ is mapped by `Resolution.toSpec` to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$. (v) For $0 < k < e$, every point $z$ in the support of $F_k$ satisfies $U(\varpi^e), V(\varpi^e) \in$ the prime ideal corresponding to the image of $z$ under `Resolution.toCrossing`. (vi) For $k < e$ there is a point lying in the supports of both $F_k$ and $F_{k+1}$. (vii) For every section $t : \operatorname{Spec} O \to$ `Resolution ϖ e` of `Resolution.toSpec` and every $d$ with $0 < d < e$ such that the image of the closed point lies in the support of $F_d$ and in the support of no other $F_k$: $t$ is a closed immersion, its kernel ideal sheaf `t.ker` is invertible in the above sense, and there exists $r \in O[u,v]/(uv-\varpi^e)$ with $\mathrm{ker}(t)\cdot\prod_k F_k^{\min(k,d)}$ equal to the ideal sheaf generated by the pullback of $r$ along `Resolution.toCrossing`.
--
--   This collects, in a single statement, the divisorial geometry of the special fibre of the toric resolution of the $A_{e-1}$-singularity $uv = \varpi^e$ over a discrete valuation ring: the components $F_k$ are effective Cartier divisors whose total sum is the divisor of $\varpi$ and whose weighted sum is the divisor of $u$, the exceptional ones lie over the vertex, consecutive ones meet, and sections meeting exactly one exceptional component are closed immersions with a controlled divisorial identity. It is used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport resolved models of modular curves, being cited by [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero) and by the corresponding chart-level statement.
